/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
# ...but DO commit the native crate's lock: the `native` CI lane builds it as a
# verified artifact, so it must resolve the exact deps (pyo3 patch) it was
# verified against, not float on every CI run.
!native/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for goldenembed: the `goldenembed` CI lane builds it (and links
# onnxruntime via `ort`), so pin the exact resolved deps it was verified against.
!goldenembed/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for goldencheck-native: the publish-goldencheck-native workflow
# builds it as a verified wheel, so pin the exact resolved deps. (goldencheck-core
# is a pyo3-free library dep -- its lock stays ignored, like graph-core; score-core
# WAS such a crate too until the tinyvec incident below promoted it to pinned.)
!goldencheck-native/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for score-wasm: build_wasm.sh produces a shipped .wasm artifact
# and wasm-bindgen-cli MUST match the exact wasm-bindgen crate version resolved
# here; a floating lock would silently produce broken JS glue at runtime.
!score-wasm/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for goldenflow-wasm: same wasm-bindgen wrapper shape as
# score-wasm, also destined to ship a built .wasm artifact via a build script.
!goldenflow-wasm/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for datafusion-udf: the python_goldenmatch CI lane builds this
# cdylib (datafusion 53 / arrow 58 / ort), so its deps must NOT float. Its lock
# was previously (mistakenly) ignored, which let a fresh resolve pull the broken
# brotli 8.0.3 (`StandardAlloc` no longer satisfies `Allocator<T>`); pinning the
# lock (brotli held at 8.0.2) keeps the verified resolve reproducible.
!datafusion-udf/Cargo.lock
# Same rationale for postgres: rust_pgrx installs and psql-smoke-tests this
# extension as a verified artifact via `cargo pgrx install` (which has no
# --locked flag to pass -- confirmed against pgrx 0.12.9's own CLI source,
# so a tracked lock is the ONLY way to pin this build), so its deps must NOT
# float. A fresh resolve on a checkout with no lock pulled tinyvec 1.13.0
# (a real upstream regression: "cannot find macro `vec` in this scope")
# where 1.12.0 -- now pinned here -- builds clean. Same incident shape as
# the datafusion-udf entry above (brotli 8.0.3 there).
!postgres/Cargo.lock
# score-core, transforms-core, fs-core and fs-wasm are pyo3-free library
# deps (no shipped artifact), so per the goldencheck-core comment above
# their locks would normally stay floating. But the `rust` job's `cargo
# test --manifest-path <crate>/Cargo.toml` step (and, for fs-wasm, the
# fixture_drift job's `wasm-pack build`) runs the SAME tinyvec-1.13.0 fresh
# resolve every required CI run repeats -- so an unpinned "library dep"
# crate can still fail a required job on any unrelated PR the moment
# crates.io's latest compatible version regresses, exactly what happened
# here (confirmed live: 2026-09-04 run 33820649810, "cannot find macro
# `vec` in this scope", same incident shape as datafusion-udf/postgres
# above). Pinning is about the CI step's reproducibility, not artifact
# shipping -- extend it to any floating crate CI directly builds or tests.
!score-core/Cargo.lock
!transforms-core/Cargo.lock
!fs-core/Cargo.lock
!fs-wasm/Cargo.lock
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.pdb
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
